<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasily II of Moscow</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1415">1415</a>–<a href="/years/1462">1462</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Vasily the Blind</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasily II was grand prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> from 1425 to 1462. His reign was dominated by a long civil war with his uncle Yuri of Galich and Yuri's sons; in 1446 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-shemyaka">Dmitry Shemyaka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-andreyevich-of-mozhaysk">Ivan of Mozhaysk</a> captured and blinded him. He recovered the throne, annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanages</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozhaysk">Mozhaysk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serpukhov">Serpukhov</a>, and left a strengthened Moscow to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow.jpg" alt="Vasily II of Moscow" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: collective · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titulyarnik_-_Vasily_Vasiliyevich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
